language ESSENCE' 1.0
$ csplib_056_sonet: an Essence' model from DCP Rosetta.
$
$ SONET: a set of nodes with traffic demands between pairs of nodes is to be installed on a set of rings. A node is installed on a ring through an add-drop multiplexer (ADM). Two nodes can communicate only if they are on at least one common ring, and each ring can host at most its capacity of nodes. Satisfy all communication demands while minimising the total number of ADMs used.
$
$ Save this file as model.eprime. Download `csplib_056_sonet.json` and `dcp_convert_essence.py` from the
$ problem's page:
$   https://dcp-bench.github.io/DCP-Rosetta/problems/csplib_056_sonet.html
$ Convert the instances once, then run the first one with Savile Row 1.11 (it needs Java); the
$ solution is written to `csplib_056_sonet_1.param.solution`:
$   python dcp_convert_essence.py csplib_056_sonet.json
$   savilerow model.eprime csplib_056_sonet_1.param -run-solver

$ n: number of nodes
given n : int
$ r: number of rings
given r : int
$ capacity_nodes[k]: the maximum number of nodes ring k can host (rings indexed 1-based)
given capacity_nodes : matrix indexed by [int(1..r)] of int
$ demand[i,j]: traffic demand between node i and node j (indices 1-based); a positive demand means the two nodes must communicate
given demand : matrix indexed by [int(1..n), int(1..n)] of int

$ ring_config[k,i]: node i is installed on ring k (indices 1-based, so the data's index 0 is the first entry)
find ring_config : matrix indexed by [int(1..r), int(1..n)] of bool
$ total_adms: the total number of ADMs used, one per node installed on a ring
find total_adms : int(0..n*r)

minimising total_adms
such that
$ the total number of ADMs is the number of node placements over all rings
total_adms = (sum k : int(1..r) . sum i : int(1..n) . toInt(ring_config[k,i])),
$ each ring hosts no more nodes than its capacity
forAll k : int(1..r) . ((sum i : int(1..n) . toInt(ring_config[k,i])) <= capacity_nodes[k]),
$ every pair of nodes with a traffic demand between them shares at least one common ring
forAll i : int(1..n) . forAll j : int(1..n) . ((i != j /\ demand[i,j] > 0) -> ((sum k : int(1..r) . toInt(ring_config[k,i]) * toInt(ring_config[k,j])) >= 1))
